faqs:
  - q: "What is a Systematic Investment Plan (SIP)?"
    a: "A Systematic Investment Plan (SIP) is an investment vehicle that allows individuals to contribute a fixed dollar amount into a mutual fund, ETF, or index portfolio at regular monthly intervals, taking advantage of rupee/dollar cost averaging and compounding returns."
  - q: "Are the returns projected by this SIP calculator guaranteed?"
    a: "No. The returns displayed are mathematical projections based strictly on your assumed annual return rate. Mutual funds and stock market securities carry market risk and returns fluctuate continuously."
  - q: "What is an annual Step-Up SIP?"
    a: "A Step-Up (or Top-Up) SIP automatically increases your monthly installment amount by a fixed percentage (e.g., 10%) once every 12 months. This mirrors annual career salary raises and substantially accelerates long-term wealth compounding."
  - q: "What is the formula for calculating SIP returns?"
    a: "The standard monthly compounding formula is: M = P × [((1 + i)^n - 1) / i] × (1 + i), where P is the periodic monthly investment, i is the periodic monthly interest rate (annual rate ÷ 1200), and n is the total number of monthly contributions."
  - q: "Is my investment plan or financial data uploaded to any server?"
    a: "No. All SIP calculations execute 100% locally in your web browser. No portfolio amounts or private financial plans are ever uploaded or tracked."
