      <h2 id="mistakes-heading">Common SIP Investing Pitfalls</h2>
      <ul style="color: var(--text-muted); line-height: 1.8; margin-left: 1.25rem;">
        <li><strong>Stopping During Market Corrections:</strong> Market pullbacks allow your fixed monthly installment to purchase mutual fund units at lower NAVs, which powers subsequent recovery gains.</li>
        <li><strong>Ignoring Expense Ratios:</strong> High fund management fees compound negatively over decades. Opt for low-cost broad index funds to keep more of your returns.</li>
        <li><strong>Treating Projections as Guarantees:</strong> Equity markets do not deliver constant geometric returns every year; annual performance fluctuates above and below historical averages.</li>
